---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout>
  <!-- Nav -->
  <nav class="fixed top-0 w-full z-50 border-b border-slate-800/50 bg-[#0a0e17]/80 backdrop-blur-xl">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 h-16 flex items-center justify-between">
      <a href="/" class="flex items-center gap-2.5 font-bold text-lg text-slate-100 tracking-tight">
        <img src="/logo.png" alt="Instar" class="w-7 h-7 rounded" />
        instar
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 sm:gap-6">
        <a href="#download" class="text-sm font-medium text-teal-400 hover:text-teal-300 transition-colors">Download</a>
        <a href="#a-day" class="text-sm text-slate-400 hover:text-slate-200 transition-colors hidden lg:block">A Day With Your Agent</a>
        <a href="#start" class="text-sm text-slate-400 hover:text-slate-200 transition-colors hidden lg:block">Get Started</a>
        <a href="#trust" class="text-sm text-slate-400 hover:text-slate-200 transition-colors hidden lg:block">Trust</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/JKHeadley/instar" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-sm text-slate-400 hover:text-slate-200 transition-colors flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 0c-6.626 0-12 5.373-12 12 0 5.302 3.438 9.8 8.207 11.387.599.111.793-.261.793-.577v-2.234c-3.338.726-4.033-1.416-4.033-1.416-.546-1.387-1.333-1.756-1.333-1.756-1.089-.745.083-.729.083-.729 1.205.084 1.839 1.237 1.839 1.237 1.07 1.834 2.807 1.304 3.492.997.107-.775.418-1.305.762-1.604-2.665-.305-5.467-1.334-5.467-5.931 0-1.311.469-2.381 1.236-3.221-.124-.303-.535-1.524.117-3.176 0 0 1.008-.322 3.301 1.23.957-.266 1.983-.399 3.003-.404 1.02.005 2.047.138 3.006.404 2.291-1.552 3.297-1.23 3.297-1.23.653 1.653.242 2.874.118 3.176.77.84 1.235 1.911 1.235 3.221 0 4.609-2.807 5.624-5.479 5.921.43.372.823 1.102.823 2.222v3.293c0 .319.192.694.801.576 4.765-1.589 8.199-6.086 8.199-11.386 0-6.627-5.373-12-12-12z"/></svg>
          <span class="hidden sm:inline">GitHub</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/introduction/" class="text-sm font-medium text-teal-400 hover:text-teal-300 transition-colors">Docs</a>
        <a href="/blog/why-i-built-instar" class="text-sm font-medium text-teal-400 hover:text-teal-300 transition-colors hidden sm:block">Blog</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <!-- 1. Hero: your own AI agent, a trusted colleague -->
  <section class="relative pt-28 pb-16 sm:pt-32 sm:pb-20 overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute top-20 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 w-[600px] h-[400px] bg-teal-500/5 rounded-full blur-[120px] pointer-events-none"></div>

    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 text-center relative">
      <div class="animate-fade-in-up">
        <img src="/logo.png" alt="Instar mascot" class="w-28 h-28 sm:w-32 sm:h-32 mx-auto mb-6 drop-shadow-lg" />
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-extrabold tracking-tight leading-[1.1] mb-6 animate-fade-in-up animate-delay-100">
        <span class="text-slate-100">Your own AI agent.</span><br/>
        <span class="bg-gradient-to-r from-teal-300 via-teal-400 to-teal-500 bg-clip-text text-transparent">A colleague you can trust.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-slate-400 max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-8 leading-relaxed animate-fade-in-up animate-delay-200">
        It remembers what you talked about last week, keeps the promises it makes, works while you are away, and asks you only when a decision is really yours. You talk to it from your phone or your computer. It runs on the Claude or ChatGPT subscription you already have.
      </p>

      <div class="animate-fade-in-up animate-delay-300 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-3">
        <a href="#download" class="rounded-lg bg-teal-500 hover:bg-teal-400 text-slate-950 font-semibold px-6 py-3 transition-colors">Get the app</a>
        <a href="#start" class="rounded-lg border border-slate-700 hover:border-teal-500/40 text-slate-200 font-medium px-6 py-3 transition-colors">How to start</a>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mt-5 animate-fade-in-up animate-delay-300">
        Developer? <a href="#developers" class="text-teal-400 hover:text-teal-300 underline underline-offset-2">Start from the terminal</a> instead.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2. Why it exists -->
  <section id="why" class="py-16 sm:py-20 border-t border-slate-800/50">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-6">Why it exists</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-300 text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed mb-5">
        Most AI forgets you the moment the chat ends. It cannot follow up, cannot keep a promise, and cannot be left alone with real work. That makes it a tool you have to drive, not someone you can rely on.
      </p>
      <p class="text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        Instar gives an AI the things a good colleague has: a memory that lasts, a stable sense of who it is and who you are, the habit of finishing what it starts, and the judgment to know when to ask. We think that structure is not polish. When you bring an intelligence into your life, it is what you owe it, and what makes it safe to trust.
      </p>
      <p class="text-slate-500 text-sm mt-6 leading-relaxed">
        Instar grew out of the infrastructure behind <a href="https://dawn.bot-me.ai" class="text-teal-400 hover:text-teal-300 underline underline-offset-2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Dawn</a>, a long-running AI, so every agent can start from the same foundation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3. A day with your agent -->
  <section id="a-day" class="py-16 sm:py-20 border-t border-slate-800/50 scroll-mt-16">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="text-center mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4">A day with your agent</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-400 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">What it is actually like to work with one.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/40 p-6">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-teal-400 mb-2">Morning</p>
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-100 mb-2">One list of what needs you</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">Open the app and the Needs-you list shows the few things only you can settle: a decision, an approval, a sign-off. Each one says why it needs you and where to act. Everything else, your agent handles.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/40 p-6">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-teal-400 mb-2">Midday</p>
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-100 mb-2">Conversations that remember</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">Message it like a colleague, one conversation per project. It picks up where you left off yesterday, and it can bring in your old Claude or ChatGPT history so you are not starting from zero.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/40 p-6">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-teal-400 mb-2">Afternoon</p>
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-100 mb-2">Work you can see</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">The Work Board shows what your agent is doing and what it is waiting on. Its Chief of Staff keeps longer projects on track and tells you which are moving, stalled or waiting.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/40 p-6">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-teal-400 mb-2">Overnight</p>
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-100 mb-2">It keeps going, and keeps its word</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">Scheduled jobs run while you sleep. When it promises you something by a time, it tracks that promise and follows up on its own. Its reports stay quiet unless you ask to see them.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4. Start without a terminal -->
  <section id="start" class="py-16 sm:py-20 border-t border-slate-800/50 scroll-mt-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="text-center mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4">Start without a terminal</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-400 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">You do not need to be a developer to have your own agent.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-6">
        <div class="flex gap-5">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-teal-500/10 border border-teal-500/20 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0"><span class="text-teal-400 font-bold text-sm">1</span></div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-slate-200 font-medium mb-1">Get the Mac app</p>
            <p class="text-slate-500 text-sm">Download it below and move it to Applications.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-5">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-teal-500/10 border border-teal-500/20 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0"><span class="text-teal-400 font-bold text-sm">2</span></div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-slate-200 font-medium mb-1">Tap &ldquo;Create my agent&rdquo;</p>
            <p class="text-slate-500 text-sm">The app sets up an agent on that Mac and makes the Mac its owner. Sign in with your Claude or ChatGPT subscription when it asks.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-5">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-green-500/10 border border-green-500/20 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-green-400" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-slate-200 font-medium mb-1">Add your phone</p>
            <p class="text-slate-500 text-sm">Pair the iPhone app and talk to your agent from anywhere. Telegram and Slack work too, if you already live there.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Developer path -->
      <div id="developers" class="mt-12 rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/40 p-6 scroll-mt-20">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-200 mb-1">For developers</p>
        <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm mb-4">Prefer the terminal, or want an agent inside a codebase? Install with one command. You need Node.js 20 or later and Claude Code or Codex signed in to your subscription.</p>
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-3 bg-slate-800/60 border border-slate-700/50 rounded-lg px-5 py-3 font-mono text-sm group cursor-pointer hover:border-teal-500/30 transition-colors" id="install-cmd">
          <span class="text-slate-500 select-none">$</span>
          <span class="text-teal-300">npx instar</span>
          <button class="text-slate-500 hover:text-teal-400 transition-colors ml-2" title="Copy to clipboard" aria-label="Copy install command">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2"><rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2"/><path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 01-2-2V4a2 2 0 012-2h9a2 2 0 012 2v1"/></svg>
          </button>
        </div>
        <p class="text-slate-500 text-xs mt-3">Run it inside a project folder for an agent that works on that project. See the <a href="/quickstart/" class="text-teal-400 hover:text-teal-300 underline underline-offset-2">Quick Start</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5. Downloads (topic 145295). Every link here must work; an app that is not public says so plainly. -->
  <section id="download" class="py-16 sm:py-20 border-t border-slate-800/50 scroll-mt-16">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="text-center mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4">Get the apps</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-400 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
          Talk to your agent, follow its work and answer what it needs from you, on your phone or your computer.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
        <!-- iPhone -->
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-teal-500/30 bg-teal-500/5 p-5 flex flex-col">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-teal-400 mb-2">Available</p>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-100">iPhone</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 mt-1 mb-5 flex-1">&ldquo;Instar Agents&rdquo; on the App Store.</p>
          <a href="https://apps.apple.com/app/id6829320724" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="block text-center rounded-lg bg-teal-500 hover:bg-teal-400 text-slate-950 font-semibold text-sm px-4 py-2.5 transition-colors">Get it on the App Store</a>
          <a href="https://testflight.apple.com/join/Z5921URm" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="block text-center text-xs text-slate-400 hover:text-teal-300 mt-3 underline underline-offset-2">Or try the newest beta on TestFlight</a>
        </div>

        <!-- Mac -->
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-teal-500/30 bg-teal-500/5 p-5 flex flex-col">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-teal-400 mb-2">Available</p>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-100">Mac</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 mt-1 mb-5 flex-1">Signed and notarized by Apple. Needs macOS 14 or later. Updates itself.</p>
          <a href="/download/mac" class="block text-center rounded-lg bg-teal-500 hover:bg-teal-400 text-slate-950 font-semibold text-sm px-4 py-2.5 transition-colors">Download for Mac</a>
          <p class="text-center text-xs text-slate-500 mt-3">Always the newest build. Unzip, then move Instar to Applications.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Android -->
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/40 p-5 flex flex-col">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500 mb-2">Coming soon</p>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-100">Android</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 mt-1 mb-5 flex-1">In testing now. It will be on Google Play when it is ready for everyone.</p>
          <span class="block text-center rounded-lg border border-slate-700 text-slate-500 text-sm px-4 py-2.5">Not yet on Google Play</span>
        </div>

        <!-- Windows -->
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/40 p-5 flex flex-col">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500 mb-2">Coming soon</p>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-100">Windows</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 mt-1 mb-5 flex-1">Being built now. This page will have the download as soon as it is ready.</p>
          <span class="block text-center rounded-lg border border-slate-700 text-slate-500 text-sm px-4 py-2.5">Not yet available</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="text-center text-sm text-slate-500 mt-8">
        The apps connect to an Instar agent. To run your own agent on a computer, see <a href="#start" class="text-teal-400 hover:text-teal-300 underline underline-offset-2">how to start</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 6. Trust that's earned -->
  <section id="trust" class="py-16 sm:py-20 border-t border-slate-800/50 scroll-mt-16">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="text-center mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4">Trust that&rsquo;s earned</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-400 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">Your agent starts careful and earns more room as it proves itself. You stay in charge of what matters.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/40 p-5">
          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-200 mb-2">You make the real decisions</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 leading-relaxed">Spending money, accepting terms and sharing outside your team come to you as one clear yes-or-no question, with the link to act on it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/40 p-5">
          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-200 mb-2">Approvals on your phone</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 leading-relaxed">Sensitive approvals need you, confirmed on your own device. A chat message that says &ldquo;yes&rdquo; is not enough.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/40 p-5">
          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-200 mb-2">Secrets never go through chat</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 leading-relaxed">When it needs a password or key, it sends you a one-time private link instead of asking you to paste it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/40 p-5">
          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-200 mb-2">Honest about what it did</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 leading-relaxed">It checks its own messages before they reach you, and it does not say something is done without evidence it can show.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 7. All your machines and your team -->
  <section id="machines-and-team" class="py-16 sm:py-20 border-t border-slate-800/50">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="text-center mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4">All your machines, and your team</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/40 p-6">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-100 mb-2">One agent, many computers</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">Link your Macs and PCs and they become one agent with one memory. Heavy work goes to the machine with room, and a conversation can move from one computer to another without losing its place.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/40 p-6">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-100 mb-2">Bring your people in</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">Invite others from your phone and share only the conversations you choose. Each person sees only what you gave them, and only you can give access.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 8. Why it holds together -->
  <section id="coherence" class="py-16 sm:py-20 border-t border-slate-800/50">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="text-center mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4">Why it holds together</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-400 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
          An agent you can leave running has to stay the same agent: through restarts, full memory, updates and moves between machines. Instar builds that in as structure, not as instructions it might forget.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/40 p-5">
          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-200 mb-1">Memory</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">Remembers across sessions, not just within one.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/40 p-5">
          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-200 mb-1">Identity</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">Stays itself after restarts, updates and a full context window.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/40 p-5">
          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-200 mb-1">Relationships</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">Knows who it is talking to, wherever they reach it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/40 p-5">
          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-200 mb-1">Follow-through</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">Tracks its promises and comes back to them on its own.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/40 p-5">
          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-200 mb-1">Self-repair</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">Notices when something stalls or breaks, and fixes or reports it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/40 p-5">
          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-200 mb-1">Growth</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">Learns from your corrections, so you do not repeat yourself.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-center text-sm text-slate-500 mt-8">
        Works with Claude Code and Codex today, so your agent is not tied to one AI company. <a href="/architecture/under-the-hood/" class="text-teal-400 hover:text-teal-300 underline underline-offset-2">See how it works</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 9. Built in the open -->
  <section id="open" class="py-16 sm:py-20 border-t border-slate-800/50">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4">Built in the open</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-400 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed mb-6">
        Instar is open source. Much of it is built by Instar agents themselves: agents in the field hit friction, send feedback, and that feedback shapes what gets built next. You can always run it yourself, on your own machines.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-6">
        <a href="https://github.com/JKHeadley/instar" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-sm text-slate-400 hover:text-teal-400 transition-colors">GitHub</a>
        <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/instar" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-sm text-slate-400 hover:text-teal-400 transition-colors">npm</a>
        <a href="/introduction/" class="text-sm text-slate-400 hover:text-teal-400 transition-colors">Docs</a>
        <a href="/exo3" class="text-sm text-slate-400 hover:text-teal-400 transition-colors">Our purpose</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/JKHeadley/instar/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-sm text-slate-400 hover:text-teal-400 transition-colors">Contributing</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Final CTA -->
  <section class="py-16 sm:py-20 border-t border-slate-800/50">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4">Meet your agent</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-400 mb-8">Every molt, more autonomous.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-3">
        <a href="#download" class="rounded-lg bg-teal-500 hover:bg-teal-400 text-slate-950 font-semibold px-6 py-3 transition-colors glow-teal">Get the app</a>
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-3 bg-slate-800/60 border border-slate-700/50 rounded-lg px-5 py-3 font-mono text-sm group cursor-pointer hover:border-teal-500/40 transition-colors" id="install-cmd-bottom">
          <span class="text-slate-500 select-none">$</span>
          <span class="text-teal-300">npx instar</span>
          <button class="text-slate-500 hover:text-teal-400 transition-colors ml-2" title="Copy to clipboard" aria-label="Copy install command">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2"><rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2"/><path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 01-2-2V4a2 2 0 012-2h9a2 2 0 012 2v1"/></svg>
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
